course: dictionary
lesson: 4798
title: Words for warm, damp air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humid means warm and damp, because there is a lot of water vapour in the air. You can find clues in the words around it. «Butterfly houses are kept warm and humid» tells you the air inside is both warm and wet, a bit like a rainforest.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «On a humid day, sweat dries slowly» makes sense if humid means damp, since wet air makes sweat dry more slowly. Humid is an adjective, and humidity is the noun for how much water vapour is in the air.
explain: Humidity is measured and given as a percentage, so a weather forecast might say the humidity is high. Scientists also use the word for things like rainforests, which have a hot, humid climate.
fact: Humid means warm and damp, with lots of water vapour in the air.
fact: Humid describes weather or a place, and humidity is the noun: the amount of water vapour in the air.
fact: Sweat cools you because, as it evaporates, it takes heat from your skin.
fact: On a humid day, sweat cannot evaporate well, so you feel hot and sticky.
fact: Humidity is measured with a hygrometer and given as a percentage.
exercise: «The rainforest was hot and humid all year.» What does humid mean? | Cold and dry, like a winter morning | Very windy and stormy | Bright and sunny | *Warm and damp, with lots of water in the air
exercise: «On a humid day, sweat dries slowly, so you feel hot and sticky.» Why do you feel hot and sticky? | You are wearing a thick coat | Your skin has turned to ice | The sun has gone behind a cloud | *Sweat does not evaporate well, so it cools you less
exercise: A weather forecast gives the humidity as a percentage. What is humidity? | How fast the wind blows | How loud the thunder is | How hot the sun is | *How much water vapour is in the air
test: «Dogs cool down by panting, but it works less well on a humid day.» Why does panting work less well when it is humid? | *The air is already full of water, so less water can evaporate | Panting makes the air drier | Dogs stop panting on humid days | The air is too cold for dogs to pant
test: Which word is the noun form of humid? | Humidly | *Humidity | Humour | Humid
exam: In «Butterfly houses are kept warm and humid», what does humid mean? | Cold and windy | Dry and dusty | *Warm and damp | Dark and quiet
